subproblem.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ and let G : ℝ^m → ℝ^P be of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1 G; ℝ^k = Euclid k). Then there are:
- a set N₀ ⊆ ℝ^P with H^m(N₀) = 0 (H^m = μHE[m]);
- sets N_l ⊆ ℝ^P (l ∈ ℕ), each an embedded m-dimensional C¹ submanifold of ℝ^P in the sense of the contract (IsEmbeddedSubmanifold 1 m N_l);
such that G(ℝ^m) ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_l N_l.
